4 9.63469Z"></path></defs><use clip-path="url(#clip_RatingStar_undefined0small)" href="#path_RatingStar_undefined0small" class="RatingStar__backgroundFill"></use><path class="RatingStar__fill"></path></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/2001286960">May 17, 2017</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">This is the second book in this new series and it’s been a turnaround for me. I read the first book thinking I wouldn’t enjoy it as much because it was about the romance between a dragon shifter and his mate. Somehow, I thought dragons as shifters were less believable than wolf shifters….. I know right?! But I totally loved it and this book was just as good.<br /><br />Boone is the wolf shifter amongst his motley crew of PIs living and working in Hawaii and he is probably the most laid back amongst the pack/weyr/clan/pride….. But when he finds Nina washed up on his section of the beach on Koa Point, the vast estate that they live, his protective streak goes into overdrive. Nina was thrown from a boat by a couple of men who tried to kill her and she has lost her memory, from the head injury she received, the shock of realising someone wanted her dead or a combination of the two. All she can remember is that her name if Nina.<br /><br />Boone carries her to the meeting house where he, Hunter and Cruz try to find out what happened to her. Silas, the leader of their group, has given strict instructions that Boone is to take her to the police the next morning but Boone has other ideas. During a ride the following day Boone and Nina, quite by chance, discover where she has been staying in Hawaii and they also discover her surname. Whilst they are off in Boone’s chalet falling in love and making a commitment to each other, Hunter does some research and the discovery of who she is was a surprise…. I can honestly say that I would never have guessed her background but unfortunately, that discovery leads her would be killers right to her.<br /><br />Although Silas and Kai are mainly absent from this book, I liked that we got to know a little bit more about Hunter and Cruz. Cruz is still scary but Hunter, it seems, is just like a cuddly teddy bear. We meet Officer Meli again and learn that although Boone seems to collect the most traffic tickets from her, it’s really Hunter she only has eyes for…. Eyes that see far too much toward the end of the book. Hunter’s story comes next and I honestly can’t wait.</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/13055353?shelf=contemporary" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">contemporary</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/13055353?shelf=dragons" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">dragons</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/13055353?shelf=paranormal" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">paranormal</span></a></span><span tabindex="-1"></span> <div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium" aria-label="Show all items in the list"><span class="Button__labelItem">...more</span></button></div></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="actions"><div class="SocialFooter__action"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium" aria-label="Review unliked. Press to like review"><span class="Button__labelItem"><i class="Icon LikeIcon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24">