2865 10.0456L7.00408 14.8432L4.40172 22.6166C4.35092 22.7683 4.37534 22.9352 4.46749 23.066C4.6275 23.2932 4.94137 23.3476 5.16853 23.1876L12 18.3758L18.8317 23.183C18.9625 23.2751 19.1293 23.2994 19.281 23.2486C19.5445 23.1604 19.6865 22.8752 19.5983 22.6117L16.996 14.8432L23.7872 10.0456C23.9206 9.95133 24 9.7981 24 9.63469Z"></path></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/1991556486">May 5, 2017</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">The second book in this new series given to us by Anna Lowe is a heart-stopper. The book continues with the saga involving five “brothers in arms”, retired from the military and at bit at odds as to what to do with their lives. Gathered by Silas and forming a family of sorts, they set up a cover as private investigators while “house sitting” for a rich benefactor. The group, comprising of two dragons, a wolf, a tiger and a bear, don’t need to look for trouble, as trouble seems to be able to find them just fine. <br />In this book, we meet Nina, a woman who has survived an attempt at murder, more or less washing up on the private shore where the fearless group reside. The moment Boone lays eyes on her, his inner wolf howls, recognizing his fated mate. But Boone is a bit more on the cautious side, having been fooled by his wolf and his human side before, even though he knows deep down that there’s something special about the unknown woman in front of him. Nina can’t remember how she got to the beach, or what she was doing, only that her first name is Nina, and that there’s a reason that she should be afraid, but when she opens her eyes and sees the hunk of a man in front of her, all she can feel is peace, warmth and safety. An inner connection that she can’t explain, but deep down, her body and heart are telling her that she can trust this man. What neither of them know is what is in store for them. Past enemies seem to resurface and memories fade and return, revealing more and more of the mysteries revolving the infamous set of “life stones” stolen from the most powerful dragon family centuries ago, each holding a special power for the beholder. <br />Ms. Lowe is a talented author, able to spin and weave the most intriguing and heart-retching tales. Her series will not disappoint, and once you start, you won’t want to miss out on any of them. This is simply another example of her wonderful talent to sweep us off to another world full of danger, suspense and love. Happy reading!<br />I received a copy of this book and am voluntarily giving my honest opinion.<br /></span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="actions"><div class="SocialFooter__action"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium" aria-label="Review unliked. Press to like review"><span class="Button__labelItem"><i class="Icon LikeIcon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M14.4813282,6.41129383 L14.586127,6.97676447 C14.5964421,7.03541935 14.6071117,7.09675198 14.6181364,7.1607667 L14.8551301,8.60363442 L17.440983,8.60363442 C18.1623576,8.60363442 18.8218187,9.01120377 19.1444272,9.65642083 L19.1708204,9.70920723 C19.4523479,10.2722622 19.4523479,10.9350066 19.1708204,11.4980616 L19.118034,11.6036344 L19.1708204,11.7092072 C19.4523479,12.2722622 19.4523479,12.9350066 19.1708204,13.4980616 L19.118034,13.6036344 L19.1708204,13.7092072 C19.4523479,14.2722622 19.4523479,14.9350066 19.1708204,15.4980616 L19,15.8397024 L19,16.1036344 C19,16.7361314 18.6701344,17.3185188 18.1373501,17.6453922 L17.9472136,17.74