 23.2932 4.94137 23.3476 5.16853 23.1876L12 18.3758L18.8317 23.183C18.9625 23.2751 19.1293 23.2994 19.281 23.2486C19.5445 23.1604 19.6865 22.8752 19.5983 22.6117L16.996 14.8432L23.7872 10.0456C23.9206 9.95133 24 9.7981 24 9.63469Z"></path></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/1994975151">May 9, 2017</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">Once again Anna Lowe has hit it out of the park with this book. I have loved everything I have read by her from Twin Moon Ranch, Blue Moon Salon, Love in Vegas, and even the Tropical getaways. Here you have not only shifters, but they are in a gorgeous locale as well.<br /><br />Book starts off with Nina getting thrown from a ship, and as she manages to rescue herself, Boone finds her washed up on the beach. As she comes too, she discovers she can't remember anything. Boone has promised her his help, even is Silas tells him to turn her over to the police.<br /><br />Boone is a wolf with a troubled past. He had thought once he had found his mate, only to have her cheat on him when he is deployed. He doesn't believe in fated mates anymore, so is trying hard to ignore his wolf claiming she is his mate.<br /><br />Digging into Nina's past brings up some shocking details, but will Boone be able to handle what they learn? If you are a fan of Paranormal Romance or Tropical getaways this is the book for you to read. I received an advanced copy of this book under no obligation to review, but can't help but let folk know this is one to pick up.</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="S